"""husk checks of texture baking against Karma's Texture Baker
(docs/design/M11-P8.md).

The scenes come from karma_bake/make_scenes.py (deterministic, standard
library; written into the output folder at test time): RenderSettings
shaped like the Karma Texture Baker LOP's (karma:global:bake_*, raw
RenderVars, the generated bake camera, one EXR per map) on analytic
meshes:
  * trace: low quads and high planes above, below and on both sides, a
    tilted low normal; trace bias/max distance and the cage offset;
  * frames: right- and left-handed low meshes with standard and mirrored
    UVs (MikkTSpace on and off);
  * slabs / ceilings: cavity, curvature (two biases), thickness, occlusion;
  * edges: edge and rounded normal across a convex and a concave
    135-degree edge;
  * pbox: the position map's boxes;
  * filters: the normal remap and the island expansion;
  * asset: a bumpy sphere baked onto a coarse one (normal, occlusion,
    curvature, cavity, thickness, height, alpha, base colour).
Karma CPU (Houdini 22.0.466) rendered the same files once; its maps are
stored below as block means (premultiplied by the coverage, as both
renderers write them). Nova (and Nova XPU, which bakes on the CPU) must
match each block within the map's tolerance; the filtered maps must equal
Nova's raw ones remapped and divided by the coverage, and every texel must
be filled.

  $HFS/python313/python.exe -I check_karma_bake.py --hfs ... --stage ... --out ...
  ... --record   renders Karma CPU instead and prints the KARMA table.
"""

